# Feature-first PRs

For feature PRs, title and body lead with what someone can demo in plain language — not stack jargon.

- **Title:** short and understandable (“Write private notes, open and edit them”), not “Add GPUI + Keychain vault”.
- **Body:** lead with the demo (what you can do, how to run, how to judge). Put crates, formats, APIs, CI, known limits under a **Technical notes** section.
- **Infra-only PRs** (CI, secrets, tooling) may stay technical — still say what changed and what it unblocks.
- Tiny copy/docs-only PRs need not be demo features.
